    "result_text": "BUILD SUCCESS \u2014 all 278 tests pass (the `createUserNoRolesFails` stack trace is expected logging from a passing negative test).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `sharesHousehold` flag on owner creation. When a new owner is created, it's set to `true` if another owner already has the same address and city, otherwise `false`. Creation is always allowed.\n\nFollowing the existing computed-field pattern (mirroring `namesakeCount`/`CountNamesakes`), since the acceptance test reads the flag back via `GET /api/owners/{id}` \u2014 which loads from the database \u2014 the value is **persisted**:\n\n1. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `Boolean sharesHousehold` field mapped to a `shares_household` column, with getter/setter.\n2. **DB schemas** (`db/{h2,hsqldb,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`) \u2014 added the `shares_household` column to the `owners` table.\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `sharesHousehold` boolean to the `Owner` schema (regenerates the `OwnerDto`; MapStruct maps it by name automatically).\n4. **`function/owner/DetermineSharesHousehold.java`** (new) \u2014 computes the flag against existing owners (case/whitespace-insensitive address+city match, excluding the owner itself), before save.\n5. **`officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the new step into the pipeline between `countNamesakes` and `save`, under the same transaction governance.",
